## 3. Typography Hierarchy & Harmonious Multi-Font Pairings

A deliberate mixture of complementary typefaces elevates brand distinction beyond single-font monotony. Global styles configure font variables (`next/font`) so different sections consume section-specific font classes:

- **Display / Heading Font (`font-display`)**: `var(--font-heading)` — [e.g. Cal Sans, Plus Jakarta Sans, Outfit, Playfair Display] + [Persian font e.g. Vazirmatn]
  - *Applied to*: Hero headlines, major section titles, and narrative callouts for distinct character.
- **Body / Interface Font (`font-sans`)**: `var(--font-sans)` — [e.g. Geist Sans, Inter] + [Persian font e.g. Vazirmatn]
  - *Applied to*: Body paragraphs, card descriptions, navigation links, and UI controls for maximum legibility.
- **Code / Monospace Font (`font-mono`)**: `var(--font-mono)` — [e.g. Geist Mono, JetBrains Mono]
  - *Applied to*: Technical metrics, status badges, overlines, and code blocks.
- **Global Section Usage**:
  - Hero & Section Titles: Consume `font-display tracking-tight font-bold`.
  - Body & Content Copy: Consume `font-sans leading-relaxed`.
  - Eyebrows & Meta Badges: Consume `font-mono tracking-wider uppercase text-xs`.

